import LOEIS.A100.A100122.Defs

set_option linter.unusedVariables false

/-!
# A100122

Decimal expansion of limit of a power tower: t(2)^(t(3)^(t(5)^(t(7)^(...)))) where t(n)=n^(1/n!) and n takes on consecutive prime values.

The 100 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A100122

/-- Known terms of `A100122`, starting at index `1`. -/
def data : List retType :=
  [1, 5, 1, 7, 7, 7, 2, 3, 6, 6,
    2, 1, 5, 2, 7, 5, 3, 9, 9, 7,
    4, 3, 3, 6, 7, 3, 3, 5, 1, 8,
    6, 9, 6, 2, 3, 2, 6, 5, 6, 0,
    7, 8, 9, 9, 8, 3, 9, 4, 6, 3,
